---
import PortfolioLayout from '../../layouts/PortfolioLayout.astro';
---

<PortfolioLayout
  title="Guilherme Rodrigues | Portfolio"
  description="Portfolio of Guilherme Rodrigues: Computer Engineering, embedded systems, IoT, applied AI, automation, projects, stories and cybersecurity."
>
  <section id="home" class="hero-section">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <h1>Guilherme Rodrigues</h1>

      <p class="hero-role">
        I'm a <span>Computer Engineering student</span>
      </p>

      <p class="hero-summary">
        A living portfolio to organize my projects, stories, studies, photos, videos and technical notes.
        Here I bring together my work with embedded systems, IoT, automation, applied artificial intelligence,
        telemetry, electronics, software and cybersecurity.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/en/projects/">View projects</a>
        <a class="btn btn-glass" href="/en/library/">Open library</a>
        <a class="btn btn-glass" href="/en/stories/">Read stories</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>About</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-copy">
      <h3>Computer Engineering, hands-on learning and hardware-software integration.</h3>

      <p>
        I am a Computer Engineering student at UTFPR, Pato Branco campus. My academic path has been built mainly
        through hands-on projects, research, outreach activities and student teams.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am especially interested in the intersection between software and hardware: embedded systems, sensors,
        telemetry, IoT, dashboards, automation, Linux, C/C++, Python, applied AI and cybersecurity.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am currently part of the Neonatal Biometrics research group at UTFPR-PB, and my undergraduate thesis focuses
        on machine learning applied to embedded platforms, evaluating neural network inference on devices such as
        Raspberry Pi.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PortfolioLayout>